{"t": 1794110154.4064806, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "[checkout] PaymentGatewayErrors (AG-7731) \u2014 cause identified, fix ready\n\nWhat: Gateway 4xx rate 38% for service=checkout since 07:41 UTC.\nCause: the payment gateway API was switched to 2026-11 (strict amounts) at 07:41 UTC. It now requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents), but checkout/gateway.py was still sending a float euro amount. Gateway response: 400 invalid_amount, \"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\".\nFix: checkout/gateway.py charge_payload() now converts EUR to integer cents (e.g. 12.34 -> 1234); currency remains EUR. Verified locally for several amounts; no change to the API field names.\nNext: deploy checkout and watch the 4xx rate on AG-7731."}, "ok": true}
